cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  analytic-prophet: Stan-free Prophet forecasting model using an analytical
  gradient instead of AutoDiff: faster and lighter on memory
abstract: >-
  Stan-free Prophet forecasting model using an analytical gradient instead
  of AutoDiff: faster and lighter on memory. It fits Prophet's model --
  verified against Stan's own log_prob -- with the log posterior and its
  gradient written out by hand and a small C++ core, so it needs no Stan
  toolchain and starts no CmdStan subprocess. It also solves an exact
  reformulation of the non-differentiable changepoint prior that Prophet's
  own optimizer stops short on, which makes its forecasts slightly better.
  Ships with a four-tier evaluation suite: a correctness gate, parameter
  recovery on synthetic series, held-out forecast accuracy on a frozen
  census of M4 weekly and daily series, and cost.
